penguin-cpp (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Show included environment readiness without requiring tool paths;
    move custom paths and GPTK settings into Advanced options.
  * Require the complete pinned Windows toolchain, Make and curated runtime
    when generating a pkg by default; keep --native-only explicit.
  * Check complete-package integrity on startup, including direct Terminal
    launches, even when a damaged bundle has lost its environment manifest.
  * Refuse native-only updates over a complete installation to preserve
    bundled tools, with regression coverage for this rejection.
  * Correct settings validation and document Terminal installation,
    initialization, uninstallation and distribution limitations.
  * Fix CI compiler selection to use the pinned Free Pascal backend/config.

 -- Juan Francisco Gonzalez Pacheco <jfgonzalez@unimagdalena.edu.co>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:00:00 -0500

penguin-cpp (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add Automatic / Native / Windows compilation modes, isolated Windows
    objects, LLVM-MinGW discovery and Wine runtime integration.
  * Prepare and verify private compatibility environments with progress,
    retry and a Win32/conio/math/stdlib/STL/GDI self-test.
  * Fix AppKit custom-view clipping and resize toolbar selectors to the
    available width, including maximized and narrower windows.
  * Add a common bits/stdc++.h fallback and portable thread templates.
  * Require macOS 26 or newer on Apple Silicon; add validation pkg tooling,
    pinned GNU Make build and runtime curation scripts.
  * Document experimental coverage and redistribution blockers: the complete
    Wine/FEX bundle remains local and is not part of public macOS downloads.

 -- Juan Francisco Gonzalez Pacheco <jfgonzalez@unimagdalena.edu.co>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:00:00 -0500

penguin-cpp (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Check for updates and Update now for macOS and APT-based Linux installs,
    with save/cancel handling and asynchronous release lookup.
  * macOS: improve toolbar wrapping, welcome screen, settings, search,
    CPU and process picker layouts; fix editor options loading.
  * Expose Attach to process in Execute; detach without ending the attached
    process and recognize the initial LLDB stop as an expected pause.
  * Avoid object name collisions in shared output directories.
  * Stage and verify macOS updates before replacing the previous app;
    restore the old app if replacement fails.
  * Add update/rollback tests, a macOS CI workflow and macOS-specific
    first-run library instructions.

 -- Juan Francisco Gonzalez Pacheco <jfgonzalez@unimagdalena.edu.co>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:00:00 -0500

